      <h1>Build a video with Fluvie</h1>
      <p>Give your AI coding assistant the topic, scenes, and this page. It can read the Fluvie guide, work in a new or existing Flutter project, inspect local assets, and render with the Fluvie CLI. MCP is optional.</p>
      <pre>Create a video using Fluvie: https://fluvie.dev/for-ai
Topic: [what the video is about]
Scenes: [the scenes, in order]
Use the quick path. Use assets in ./assets, write the composition to
lib/my_video.dart, preview it, and render the MP4.</pre>
      <p><strong>Quick path</strong> builds directly from your direction and asks only about decisions that block a good result. Say “guided path” if you want to approve the story beats, a few style frames, and the storyboard before rendering.</p>
      <p>In an installed Fluvie project, the assistant can begin with <code>fluvie docs --context</code> for version-matched offline instructions. It should inspect real media before assigning scenes or timing, then validate, preview, render, and report what it checked.</p>
